ech 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490469} {:answer/id #uuid "eca5ccfb-5a6d-5e3c-a029-83d13447b009" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}(\\tanh 2 - \\tanh 8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79d933d5-1669-580f-9d24-03050414e7e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}(\\sech 8 - \\sech 16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490442} :answer-field/id #uuid "855d3e32-94d6-58b4-bf61-bd748743b8b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490447}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a020bcec-f970-5078-a5eb-2d608546029d" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\int_{1}^{2}\\sech 8x\\tanh 8x\\,\\mathrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=8x$. Then $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{8}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. When $x=1$, $u=8$; when $x=2$, $u=16$.\n\nUsing $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\sech u=-\\sech u\\tanh u$,\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_1^2\\sech(8x)\\tanh(8x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=\\frac{1}{8}\\int_{8}^{16}\\sech u\\tanh u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{8}[-\\sech u]_{8}^{16} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{8}(\\sech 8-\\sech 16).\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe integrand is continuous on $[1,2]$, and the result is positive because $\\sech u$ decreases for $u>0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490461 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "355ee97e-2d9d-513c-af30-19d7946e5740" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\tanh (\\frac{5x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490426} {:answer/id #uuid "7bf6b45f-ddee-5619-98e3-65ad83574b62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\csch^{2} (\\frac{5x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490443} {:answer/id #uuid "9ac28e6c-80dd-5da7-b9d8-4fcc754864fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\tanh (\\frac{5x}{5})\\sech (\\frac{5x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490454} {:answer/id #uuid "b71279ad-1d95-5961-8910-c4a7b04f5a28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\tanh (\\frac{5x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490465} {:answer/id #uuid "f47af739-648c-5d6e-becf-e5d608136d60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\tanh^{2} (\\frac{5x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b71279ad-1d95-5961-8910-c4a7b04f5a28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\tanh (\\frac{5x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490465} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae38fbbc-5bf2-5219-ab70-662a16f02eb9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490460}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aec90261-3e41-5113-be2e-aad35ddf754d" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\int\\sech^{2} (\\frac{5x}{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{5x}{5}$. Differentiating gives $\\mathrm{d}u=1\\,\\mathrm{d}x$, so $\\mathrm{d}x=1\\,\\mathrm{d}u$.\n\nUsing the substitution and $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\tanh u=\\sech^2 u$,\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\sech^2(\\frac{5x}{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=1\\int\\sech^2 u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=1\\tanh u+C \\\\\n&=1\\tanh(\\frac{5x}{5})+C.\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe argument is linear and the integrand is defined for every real $x$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490468 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "030c3210-41d0-5d61-908e-6a5256cd4f8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}\\tanh (\\frac{6x}{5})\\sech (\\frac{6x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490413} {:answer/id #uuid "1a7625a0-da78-5b93-988d-411851e95bf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}\\tanh^{2} (\\frac{6x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490416} {:answer/id #uuid "4e90ae45-661d-54de-a0ba-beeb24ace4e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}\\tanh (\\frac{6x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490431} {:answer/id #uuid "7f134b14-df14-5b6f-8f49-59aa902f5ed5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\tanh (\\frac{5x}{6}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490444} {:answer/id #uuid "f313c669-3bcc-5d7a-8bcb-6c8ac49990b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{6}\\csch^{2} (\\frac{6x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e90ae45-661d-54de-a0ba-beeb24ace4e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}\\tanh (\\frac{6x}{5}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490431} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce095602-03dd-5b07-943d-af6c81a7c8d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490471}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bfb61a77-a546-509b-9714-acf060d2c17a" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\int\\sech^{2} (\\frac{6x}{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{6x}{5}$. Differentiating gives $\\mathrm{d}u=\\frac{6}{5}\\,\\mathrm{d}x$, so $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{5}{6}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$.\n\nUsing the substitution and $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\tanh u=\\sech^2 u$,\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\sech^2(\\frac{6x}{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=\\frac{5}{6}\\int\\sech^2 u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=\\frac{5}{6}\\tanh u+C \\\\\n&=\\frac{5}{6}\\tanh(\\frac{6x}{5})+C.\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe argument is linear and the integrand is defined for every real $x$."}] :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions With Linear Arguments"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166786 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166624 :question/id #uuid "adec9fbb-c33d-5557-b1cd-dfd42d6c594d" :question/math-academy-id "e-8407" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral\n$\\displaystyle \\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits} {\\displaystyle \\int_{-2}^{2} x^2\\sinh{x^3}}\\, \\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=x^3$. Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=3x^2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac{1}{3}\\textrm{d} u = x^2\\, \\textrm d x\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u$.\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x & -2 & 2 \\\\ u & -8 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits} \\int_{-2}^{2} x^2\\sinh{x^3}\\, \\textrm{d}x &=\\int_{-2}^{2} \\sinh{x^3}\\cdot x^2\\,\\textrm{d}x \\\\[5pt] &=\\int_{-8}^{8} \\sinh{u}\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{3}\\, \\textrm{d}u \\\\[5pt] &=\\left.\\dfrac{1}{3}\\cosh u\\Big\\right|_{-8}^{8} \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(\\cosh{8} - \\cosh{(-8)}\\right) \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(\\cosh{8} - \\cosh{8}\\right) \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\cdot 0 \\\\[5pt] &=0 \\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "947ecbc7-e09a-58b6-916d-a2562a1e794a" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049713 :topic/math-academy-id 1362 :topic/title "Differentiating Hyperbolic Functions"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167384 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91492421-4e01-5746-b0f8-1d9e6810c2a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\sinh (x^{2}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165513} {:answer/id #uuid "9a85bf73-4ea9-5b6f-890d-b9b888e13dcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\sinh (2x^{2}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165514} {:answer/id #uuid "ccd1e07e-8080-5758-ae18-442b44314a3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}\\sinh (2x^{2}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165515} {:answer/id #uuid "2843d3bd-59e1-5c05-be99-50316de0ad0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\sinh (x^{2}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165516} {:answer/id #uuid "47b9e4e1-6df1-54a4-b59e-36da8f0d3bef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\sinh (4x^{2}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165517}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f91f8f8f-2b58-5bb5-ad72-8607b411262c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165512}] :question/id #uuid "ee28a08c-e134-5d5e-b82d-9846325c8068" :question/math-academy-id "q-95537" :question/problem "Calculate $\\intx\\cosh (2x^{2})dx$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167385 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d1421ab6-995f-5597-a20e-0bf5221365c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1 - 2e}{e^{2} + 1}" :d