field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e559296-77e3-5ce6-9097-3e91f43b48e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}\\ln \\mid 4\\coth x + 1 \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482730} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f79df49-f55f-5434-bbe8-e27ec72c9856" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482756}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae74f884-ae1a-5c74-b1db-3a06095c05ad" :question/problem "What is $\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\displaystyle \\int\\frac{\\csch^{2} x}{4\\coth x + 1}dx$?" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nLet $u=4\\coth x+1$. Differentiating gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-4\\csch^2 x,\n\\qquad \\csch^2 x\\,\\mathrm{d}x=-\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.$$\n\nUsing this substitution, we obtain\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{\\csch^2 x}{4\\coth x+1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}\\int\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}\\ln|u|+C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}\\ln|4\\coth x+1|+C.\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe antiderivative is valid on each interval where $x\\ne0$ and $4\\coth x+1\\ne0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482780 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3db46bb1-ac6e-54c4-9ebe-35705f6a58cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\ln (\\frac{16}{17})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482740} {:answer/id #uuid "472e87e4-74c1-5005-8c9a-a499a58a14f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln (\\frac{3}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482746} {:answer/id #uuid "c3d0cde4-f50b-56fe-b792-ac8221f724ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln (\\frac{4}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482782} {:answer/id #uuid "dde17509-aaa7-56ca-ae80-5ab124f69c2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482787} {:answer/id #uuid "e946d67f-0c85-5adc-8926-5cb176fa01f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln (\\frac{13}{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e946d67f-0c85-5adc-8926-5cb176fa01f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln (\\frac{13}{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482789} :answer-field/id #uuid "3eacd647-34b8-5d12-b736-6395fc30e69a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482742}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c05537f7-1d5d-5292-9d77-e4dd0daf2542" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral\n$\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{\\ln 4}\\frac{\\cosh x}{3 + \\sinh x}dx$." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=3+\\sinh x$. Differentiating gives $\\mathrm{d}u=\\cosh x\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nWhen $x=0$, $u=3$. When $x=\\ln 4$,\n\n$$u=3+\\frac{e^{\\ln 4}-e^{-\\ln 4}}{2}\n=3+\\frac{4-\\frac{1}{4}}{2}=\\frac{39}{8}.$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_0^{\\ln 4}\\frac{\\cosh x}{3+\\sinh x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=\\int_3^{\\frac{39}{8}}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=\\left[\\ln u\\right]_3^{\\frac{39}{8}} \\\\\n&=\\ln(\\frac{39}{8})-\\ln 3 \\\\\n&=\\ln\\left(\\frac{13}{8}\\right).\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nHere $u>0$ throughout the interval, so the logarithm and substitution are defined."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482784 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4864266c-e5e5-515b-96a0-ab9e8b35f984" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}\\ln \\mid 6\\coth x + 1 \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482747} {:answer/id #uuid "59ee84ab-2073-532b-8046-9ef988b617f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\ln \\mid 6\\csch^{2} x + 1 \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482749} {:answer/id #uuid "a6f5d408-6e65-55f